  "term": "attentiveness",
  "definition": "Attentiveness is the inward focusing of consciousness on a stimulus or idea so that it becomes more clearly perceived. In this historical account, it involves an active mental adjustment to the strength and kind of what is being noticed, often accompanied by a felt sense of effort or strain.",
